cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or benchmark artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Negative-Space Search v0.7: Search Governance, Not Discovery"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Janson
    given-names: Björn
version: "0.7"
date-released: 2026-08-07
repository-code: "https://github.com/bjoern-janson/negative-space-search"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An experimental benchmark program investigating whether systems can detect
  when their current representational structures are inadequate and selectively
  allocate expansion effort. The v0.7 release evaluates boundary-gated
  representational repair against always-expand generic synthesis baselines.
  The supported contribution is search governance and adaptive representational
  economy, not superior invention or autonomous discovery.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - adaptive systems
  - representation learning
  - epistemology
  - causal reasoning
  - model uncertainty
  - search governance
  - corrigibility
